{"study_accession":"PRJNA787790","secondary_study_accession":"SRP350209","title":"Human FcgRIIa mediates attenuation of IFN-I response in human monocytes","description":"It is generally believed that there is continued cross-regulation between adaptive humoral immunity and Type I interferon (IFN-I) response during viral infections, but the question how antibodies (Abs), and/or Ab-antigen immunocomplexes (ICs), regulate IFN-I production and/or signaling in immune cells remains unanswered. Here we report that plate-coated IgG (cIgG), a mimic IC without antigen restriction, could dampen IFN-I signaling in monocytes through FcgRIIa. Overall design: Freshly isolated CD14+ monocytes from peripheral blood of 3 unrelated healthy donors  were cultured for 24 hrs in RPMI-10 medium or IVIG(10 μg/ml) for preparation, then half of these cultures were washed and given a 12 hrs IFN-alpha or IFN-beta (10 ng/mL) stimulation,respectively.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":15,"study_labels":[{"level":"study","event_code":"ACUTE_VIRAL_INFECTION","certainty":"suspected","delta_days":null,"delta_bucket":"UNK","time_precision":"unknown","stage":"teacher","confidence":1.0,"evidence":"tes It is generally believed that there is continued cross-regulation between adaptive humoral immunity and Type I interferon (IFN-I) response during viral infections, but the question how antibodies (Abs), and/or Ab-antigen immunocomplexes (ICs), regulate IFN-I production and/or signaling in immune","model_version":"teacher:mlx:mlx-community/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct-4bit"}],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN23846377","study_accession":"PRJNA787790","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"Mo(RPMI)_rep1","description":"Mo(RPMI)_rep1","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5726762","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2024-12-12","attributes":[["source_name","Monocytes"],["donor","donor_id: 1"],["cell_type","Peripheral blood monuclear cells"],["compound","stimulated with: none"]],"run